I go to the front desk of the club.
A person is sitting there.
I smile at him.
"Are you a member here?" he asks.
"No, I am not a member," I reply.
"Can I play for one day?" I ask.
"Yes, you can play," he says.
"The guest fee is two hundred rupees."
I give him two hundred rupees.
But I do not have a racket with me.
"Can I take a racket on rent?" I ask.
"Yes, you can," he replies.
"The rent for the racket is fifty rupees."
I give fifty rupees more.
He gives me a good racket.
"Thank you," I tell him.
Now, I am going to play.
